```
     1→_ulid: 01KF1XMETA0000000000000000
     2→slugs:
     3→  - meta
     4→  - meta-spec
     5→  - meta-module
     6→title: Meta-Spec System
     7→type: module
     8→status:
     9→  maturity: draft
    10→  implementation: implemented
    11→description: |
    12→  Meta-spec is the layer that defines HOW work happens, separate from
    13→  WHAT is being built (spec) and tracking WORK (tasks).
    14→
    15→  The key distinction:
    16→  - Spec: What to build (features, requirements)
    17→  - Tasks: Work to do (implement feature X)
    18→  - Meta-spec: How to work (check spec before implementing)
    19→
    20→  Meta-spec enables a self-improvement loop:
    21→  1. Define workflows → 2. Track adherence → 3. Identify friction →
    22→  4. Propose improvements → 5. Update workflows → (repeat)
    23→
    24→  Meta-spec complements prose docs (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md) rather than
    25→  replacing them. Structured definitions + prose guidance work together.
    26→features:
    27→  - _ulid: 01KF1XMNF00000000000000000
    28→    slugs:
    29→      - meta-manifest
    30→      - meta-file
    31→    title: Meta Manifest
    32→    type: feature
    33→    status:
    34→      maturity: draft
    35→      implementation: implemented
    36→    priority: high
    37→    tags:
    38→      - mvp
    39→      - meta
    40→    description: |
    41→      The meta manifest (kynetic.meta.yaml) is the root file for process
    42→      definitions. It lives alongside kynetic.yaml and defines agents,
    43→      workflows, conventions, and observations.
    44→
    45→      Unlike spec items which define product features, meta items define
    46→      how work is done on the project.
    47→    acceptance_criteria:
    48→      - id: ac-meta-manifest-1
    49→        given: a project with kynetic.yaml
    50→        when: kynetic.meta.yaml is created with valid structure
    51→        then: >
    52→          kspec meta show outputs summary with counts for agents, workflows, conventions, and
    53→          observations (exit code 0)
    54→      - id: ac-meta-manifest-2
    55→        given: a meta manifest exists
    56→        when: kspec validate runs
    57→        then: >
    58→          output includes "Meta: X agents, Y workflows, Z conventions" line; validation errors for
    59→          meta items use "meta:" prefix to distinguish from spec errors
    60→      - id: ac-meta-manifest-3
    61→        given: kynetic.meta.yaml has invalid schema
    62→        when: kspec validate runs
    63→        then: >
    64→          exits with code 1; error message identifies the invalid field path and expected type
    65→          (e.g., "meta:agents[0].capabilities: expected array")
    66→    requirements:
    67→      - _ulid: 01KF1XMNF10000000000000000
    68→        slugs:
