   312→        when: workflows are defined
   313→        then: >
   314→          outputs each workflow with full step list; steps show type prefix ([check], [action],
   315→          [decision]) and content; on_fail shown for checks
   316→      - id: ac-workflow-3
   317→        given: a workflow reference @workflow-id is used in meta_ref
   318→        when: kspec validate runs
   319→        then: >
   320→          validates reference resolves to a workflow definition; error message shows "meta_ref must
   321→          point to workflow, agent, or convention"
   322→      - id: ac-workflow-4
   323→        given: kspec meta workflows --json runs
   324→        when: workflows are defined
   325→        then: >
   326→          outputs JSON array with objects containing: id, trigger, description, steps (array of
   327→          {type, content, on_fail?})
   328→    requirements:
   329→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF10000000000000000
   330→        slugs:
   331→          - workflow-schema
   332→        title: Workflow Schema
   333→        type: requirement
   334→        status:
   335→          maturity: draft
   336→          implementation: not_started
   337→        description: |
   338→          Workflow definition structure:
   339→
   340→          ```yaml
   341→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   342→            id: spec-first         # Short identifier
   343→            trigger: behavior change
   344→            description: |
   345→              Check spec coverage before implementing changes.
   346→            steps:
   347→              - type: check
   348→                content: Does the spec cover this change?
   349→                on_fail: Update spec first
   350→              - type: action
   351→                content: Update spec if needed
   352→              - type: action
   353→                content: Derive task from spec
   354→              - type: action
   355→                content: Implement the change
   356→          ```
   357→
   358→          Steps have types: check, action, decision
   359→          on_fail provides guidance when checks fail.
   360→        implements:
   361→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   362→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   363→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF20000000000000000
   364→        slugs:
   365→          - workflow-steps
   366→        title: Workflow Step Types
   367→        type: requirement
   368→        status:
   369→          maturity: draft
   370→          implementation: not_started
   371→        description: |
   372→          Step types:
   373→
   374→          - check: Verification step (pass/fail)
   375→            Has on_fail for what to do if check fails
   376→
   377→          - action: Something to do
   378→            No conditional, just execute
   379→
   380→          - decision: Branch point
   381→            Has options for different paths
   382→
   383→          Steps are executed in order. Agents interpret them,
   384→          they're not automatically enforced.
   385→        implements:
   386→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   387→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   388→      - _ulid: 01KF2XWKF40000000000000000
   389→        slugs:
   390→          - workflow-execution-model
   391→        title: Workflow Execution Model
   392→        type: requirement
   393→        status:
   394→          maturity: draft
   395→          implementation: not_started
   396→        description: |
   397→          Workflows are ADVISORY, not AUTOMATED. This is a deliberate design choice.
   398→
   399→          Execution model options:
   400→
   401→          1. **Documentation** (default): Workflows exist as reference documentation.
   402→             Agents read them when relevant, but no runtime enforcement.
   403→             `kspec meta workflows` displays them for human/agent reference.
   404→
   405→          2. **Checklist**: Workflows can be displayed as interactive checklists.
   406→             `kspec meta run @workflow` presents steps one at a time,
   407→             agent confirms each step completion. Progress tracked but not enforced.
   408→
   409→          3. **Hook integration**: Workflows can inform Claude Code hooks.
   410→             A hook could query `kspec meta workflows --trigger "commit"`
   411→             and inject relevant workflow steps into the prompt.
   412→             Still advisory - hook provides context, agent decides.
   413→
   414→          Why not automation?
   415→          - Workflows describe nuanced processes that require judgment
   416→          - "Check if spec covers this" can't be reliably automated
   417→          - Automation creates brittleness; advisory enables adaptation
   418→          - Trust agents to follow documented processes
   419→
   420→          Future: Workflow adherence tracking via observations.
   421→          Friction observations on workflows indicate where guidance fails.
   422→          This creates a feedback loop: observe friction → improve workflow.
   423→
   424→          ```yaml
   425→          # Optional execution hints
   426→          steps:
   427→            - type: check
   428→              content: Does the spec cover this change?
   429→              on_fail: Update spec first
   430→              execution:
   431→                mode: prompt  # prompt, silent, or skip
   432→                timeout: null # Optional timeout for automated checks
   433→          ```
   434→
   435→          execution.mode values:
   436→          - prompt (default): Show step, wait for confirmation
   437→          - silent: Log step, don't wait
   438→          - skip: Skip in checklist mode (documentation only)
   439→        implements:
   440→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   441→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   442→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF30000000000000000
   443→        slugs:
