   563→      - _ulid: 01KF2XCNV30000000000000000
   564→        slugs:
   565→          - convention-validation
   566→        title: Convention Validation Strategy
   567→        type: requirement
   568→        status:
   569→          maturity: draft
   570→          implementation: not_started
   571→        description: |
   572→          Conventions support optional validation with domain-specific strategies:
   573→
   574→          ```yaml
   575→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   576→            domain: commits
   577→            rules:
   578→              - Use conventional commit format
   579→            validation:
   580→              type: regex
   581→              pattern: "^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore)(\\(.+\\))?:\\s.+"
   582→              message: "Commit must follow conventional format"
   583→          ```
   584→
   585→          Validation types by domain:
   586→
   587→          - commits: regex pattern matching on message
   588→          - notes: word count range, required sections
   589→          - naming: regex pattern for slugs/identifiers
   590→          - tags: enum list of allowed tags
   591→          - branching: regex pattern for branch names
   592→          - documentation: prose (advisory only, no automation)
   593→
   594→          Validation configuration:
   595→
   596→          ```yaml
   597→          validation:
   598→            type: regex | enum | range | prose
   599→            # For regex:
   600→            pattern: "^pattern$"
   601→            message: "Error message when validation fails"
   602→            # For enum:
   603→            allowed: [value1, value2, value3]
   604→            # For range:
   605→            min: 10
   606→            max: 500
   607→            unit: words | chars | lines
   608→          ```
   609→
   610→          Validation is optional - conventions without validation field
   611→          are advisory-only and appear in documentation.
   612→
   613→          `kspec validate --conventions` runs all validatable conventions.
   614→          Prose-type conventions are skipped with info message.
   615→        implements:
   616→          - '@convention-definitions'
   617→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
