   619→  - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK00000000000000000
   620→    slugs:
   621→      - observations
   622→      - feedback-loop
   623→    title: Observations
   624→    type: feature
   625→    status:
   626→      maturity: draft
   627→      implementation: implemented
   628→    priority: high
   629→    tags:
   630→      - mvp
   631→      - meta
   632→      - feedback
   633→    description: |
   634→      Observations capture feedback about workflows and conventions.
   635→      This is the mechanism for the self-improvement loop - agents
   636→      record friction, success, questions, and ideas, then patterns
   637→      emerge that inform workflow improvements.
   638→
   639→      Observations can be promoted to tasks with --meta-ref, creating
   640→      trackable work to improve processes.
   641→    acceptance_criteria:
   642→      - id: ac-obs-1
   643→        given: an agent encounters workflow friction
   644→        when: kspec meta observe friction "description" runs
   645→        then: >
   646→          outputs "OK Created observation: <ULID-prefix>"; observation stored with fields: _ulid,
   647→          type, content, created_at (ISO8601), author, resolved (false), workflow_ref (if --workflow
   648→          provided)
   649→      - id: ac-obs-2
   650→        given: observations exist
   651→        when: kspec meta observations runs
   652→        then: >
   653→          outputs table with columns: ID, Type, Workflow, Created, Content (truncated); shows only
   654→          unresolved by default; --all includes resolved
   655→      - id: ac-obs-3
   656→        given: an observation exists
   657→        when: kspec meta promote @obs --title "Task title" runs
   658→        then: >
   659→          creates task with: title from --title, description from observation content, meta_ref from
   660→          observation's workflow_ref; outputs "OK Created task: <ULID-prefix>"; observation updated
   661→          with promoted_to field pointing to new task
   662→      - id: ac-obs-4
   663→        given: an observation exists
   664→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs "resolution text" runs
   665→        then: >
   666→          observation updated with: resolved=true, resolution=text, resolved_at (ISO8601),
   667→          resolved_by (author); outputs "OK Resolved: <ULID-prefix>"
   668→      - id: ac-obs-5
   669→        given: kspec meta observations --json runs
   670→        when: observations exist
   671→        then: |
   672→          outputs JSON array with full observation objects including all fields
   673→      - id: ac-obs-6
   674→        given: an observation has already been promoted (has promoted_to field)
   675→        when: kspec meta promote @obs runs
   676→        then: >
   677→          exits with code 1; error message: "Observation already promoted to task <task-ref>;
   678→          resolve or delete the task first"
   679→      - id: ac-obs-7
   680→        given: an observation is already resolved (resolved=true)
   681→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs runs
   682→        then: >
   683→          exits with code 1; error message: "Observation already resolved on <date>:
   684→          '<resolution-text-truncated>'"
   685→      - id: ac-obs-8
   686→        given: an observation is already resolved
   687→        when: kspec meta promote @obs runs
   688→        then: >
   689→          exits with code 1; error message: "Cannot promote resolved observation; use --force to
   690→          override"
   691→      - id: ac-obs-9
   692→        given: an observation has promoted_to pointing to a completed task
   693→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs runs with no explicit resolution
   694→        then: >
   695→          auto-populates resolution from task completion reason if available; prompts for resolution
   696→          text if task has no completion reason
   697→    requirements:
   698→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK10000000000000000
   699→        slugs:
   700→          - observation-schema
   701→        title: Observation Schema
   702→        type: requirement
   703→        status:
   704→          maturity: draft
   705→          implementation: not_started
   706→        description: |
   707→          Observation structure:
   708→
   709→          ```yaml
   710→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   711→            type: friction        # friction, success, question, idea
   712→            workflow_ref: "@spec-first"  # Related workflow (optional)
   713→            content: |
   714→              Spec-first check feels heavyweight for typo fixes.
   715→              Interrupts flow for trivial changes.
   716→            created_at: "2025-01-15T10:00:00Z"
   717→            author: "@claude"
   718→            resolved: false
   719→            resolution: null      # Filled when resolved
   720→          ```
   721→
   722→          Types capture the nature of the feedback.
   723→          workflow_ref links to relevant workflow for tracking.
   724→        implements:
   725→          - '@observations'
   726→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   727→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK20000000000000000
   728→        slugs:
   729→          - observation-types
   730→        title: Observation Types
   731→        type: requirement
   732→        status:
   733→          maturity: draft
   734→          implementation: not_started
   735→        description: |
   736→          Observation types:
   737→
   738→          - friction: Something that's hard, slow, or frustrating
   739→          - success: Something that works well (positive feedback)
   740→          - question: Uncertainty about how to proceed
   741→          - idea: Potential improvement or new approach
   742→
   743→          All types feed the improvement loop. Friction and ideas
   744→          most often lead to workflow changes. Success confirms
   745→          what's working. Questions may reveal documentation gaps.
   746→        implements:
   747→          - '@observations'
   748→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   749→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK30000000000000000
   750→        slugs:
   751→          - observation-promotion
   752→        title: Observation Promotion
   753→        type: requirement
   754→        status:
   755→          maturity: draft
   756→          implementation: not_started
   757→        description: |
   758→          Observations can be promoted to tasks:
   759→
   760→          ```bash
   761→          kspec meta promote @obs-123 \
   762→            --title "Simplify spec-first for trivial changes" \
   763→            --priority 2
   764→          ```
   765→
   766→          Creates task with:
   767→          - title from --title
   768→          - meta_ref pointing to related workflow
   769→          - description from observation content
   770→          - origin: observation_promotion
   771→
   772→          Original observation marked with promoted_to reference.
   773→        implements:
   774→          - '@observations'
   775→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   776→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK40000000000000000
   777→        slugs:
   778→          - observation-resolution
   779→        title: Observation Resolution
   780→        type: requirement
   781→        status:
   782→          maturity: draft
   783→          implementation: not_started
   784→        description: |
   785→          Resolving observations:
   786→
   787→          ```bash
   788→          kspec meta resolve @obs-123 "Addressed by --quick flag in v0.2"
   789→          ```
   790→
   791→          Sets:
   792→          - resolved: true
   793→          - resolution: "Addressed by --quick flag in v0.2"
   794→          - resolved_at: timestamp
   795→          - resolved_by: author
   796→
   797→          Resolved observations remain for history.
   798→          Unresolved observations show in session context.
   799→        implements:
   800→          - '@observations'
   801→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   802→      - _ulid: 01KF2XFBK50000000000000000
   803→        slugs:
   804→          - observation-task-loop
   805→        title: Observation-Task Resolution Loop
   806→        type: requirement
   807→        status:
   808→          maturity: draft
   809→          implementation: not_started
   810→        description: |
   811→          The observation→task→resolution loop defines how observations connect
   812→          to tasks and when they get resolved.
   813→
   814→          **Promotion creates linkage**:
   815→          When an observation is promoted to a task:
   816→          - observation.promoted_to = @task-ref
   817→          - task.origin = "observation_promotion"
   818→          - task.description includes observation content
   819→
   820→          **Task completion does NOT auto-resolve**:
   821→          Completing a task does not automatically resolve linked observations.
   822→          This is intentional:
   823→          - Task might address the observation partially
   824→          - Multiple tasks might be needed
   825→          - Agent should explicitly confirm resolution
   826→
   827→          **Explicit resolution required**:
   828→          After completing the task, agent runs:
   829→          ```bash
   830→          kspec meta resolve @obs "Addressed by task @task-ref"
   831→          ```
   832→
   833→          **Convenience: resolve-from-task**:
   834→          If observation has promoted_to pointing to a completed task:
   835→          ```bash
   836→          kspec meta resolve @obs
   837→          # Auto-populates: "Resolved via task @task-ref: <task.reason>"
   838→          ```
   839→          Prompts for resolution text if task has no completion reason.
   840→
   841→          **Session context reminder**:
   842→          When task with origin="observation_promotion" is completed,
   843→          session context shows reminder:
   844→          "Consider resolving linked observation: @obs-ref"
   845→
   846→          **Querying the loop**:
   847→          ```bash
   848→          # Find observations that spawned tasks
   849→          kspec meta observations --promoted
   850→
   851→          # Find tasks from observations
   852→          kspec tasks list --origin observation_promotion
   853→
   854→          # Find unresolved observations with completed tasks
   855→          kspec meta observations --pending-resolution
   856→          ```
   857→
   858→          This explicit loop ensures observations aren't lost when tasks
   859→          complete, and creates traceable process improvement history.
   860→        implements:
   861→          - '@observations'
   862→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
   863→    created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
