  1474→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
  1475→      - _ulid: 01KF2XREF40000000000000000
  1476→        slugs:
  1477→          - meta-ref-validation
  1478→        title: Meta Reference Validation
  1479→        type: requirement
  1480→        status:
  1481→          maturity: draft
  1482→          implementation: not_started
  1483→        description: |
  1484→          meta_ref field validation rules:
  1485→
  1486→          1. **Reference must resolve**: The @ref must point to an existing item
  1487→             Error: "meta_ref '@xyz' does not resolve to any item"
  1488→
  1489→          2. **Reference must be meta item**: The resolved item must be a meta
  1490→             item (agent, workflow, convention), not a product spec item.
  1491→             Error: "meta_ref '@xyz' points to spec item; use --spec-ref instead"
  1492→
  1493→          3. **Type hints** (optional): For stricter validation, meta_ref can
  1494→             specify expected type:
  1495→             ```yaml
  1496→             meta_ref:
  1497→               ref: "@spec-first"
  1498→               type: workflow  # Validates ref is a workflow
  1499→             ```
  1500→             Error: "meta_ref '@xyz' expected workflow, got agent"
  1501→
  1502→          4. **Validation timing**: Checked on:
  1503→             - `kspec task add --meta-ref`
  1504→             - `kspec validate` (full validation)
  1505→             - `kspec task set --meta-ref` (updates)
  1506→
  1507→          5. **Circular reference prevention**: meta_ref cannot point to
  1508→             the task itself or create reference cycles.
  1509→
  1510→          Implementation: Validation uses the same reference resolution
  1511→          as spec_ref, but filters for meta item types. Meta items are
  1512→          identified by their source file (kynetic.meta.yaml or meta/ includes)
  1513→          or by explicit type markers.
  1514→        implements:
  1515→          - '@meta-ref'
  1516→        created: '2026-01-17T05:46:34.849Z'
